# Type Discipline

## Reuse canonical types

Before adding an interface or type:

- search for the proposed name and close synonyms;
- search for its distinctive fields;
- prefer the shared process, IPC, service-channel, or engine type that already
  represents the contract;
- keep renderer/service contracts under `src/shared/types/`.

Do not create a layer-specific copy of an existing payload shape.

## Export only when imported

- Keep file-local types unexported.
- Inline one-off channel request or response shapes.
- Remove `export` when the final external import is removed.
- Import from the defining module; do not add convenience re-exports.

## Consolidate completely

When replacing or moving a type, remove the superseded definition and all of
its imports in the same change. Do not leave aliases or compatibility shims.
